                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7677dc85-5b63-3c4d-abcb-e82c9c4c2354",
                        "entry_id": "77826447-dda7-3df5-91ee-f659ae59f58a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère correspondant à une notion comme un idéogramme et au son comme un phonogramme en même temps."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32806226-d5eb-398f-9d9b-7a98982925e3",
                        "entry_id": "77826447-dda7-3df5-91ee-f659ae59f58a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sinogramme composé de deux caractères plus simples, l’un pour le radical de la catégorie sémantique et l’autre pour la prononciation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c03d4ae-19ba-41ec-a91e-b722174d9481",
                                "sense_id": "32806226-d5eb-398f-9d9b-7a98982925e3",
                                "text": "La structure par laquelle la figure se situe à la gauche et le son se situe à la droite est la structure la plus essentielle et la plus courante de l’idéophonogramme. […] N’importe quel idéophonogramme de cette catégorie, celui de 妈 (ma, mère ou plus précisément ma de maman) par exemple, se compose de deux pictogrammes. La gauche est 女 le pictogramme de femme et la droite 马 le pictogramme de cheval."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "11370d74-5db4-4a9d-8a9d-861093cec3d3",
                        "source_entry_id": "77826447-dda7-3df5-91ee-f659ae59f58a",
                        "target_lang_word": "phono-semantic compound",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "phono-semantic compound",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca04ff37-2cae-3020-93fe-11b2d3666afa",
                                        "entry_id": "4a90a279-d0f1-353c-97e4-9ea26739201c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A Chinese character (CJKV character) composed of a component which is related to the meaning the character and another component which is related to the sound of the character."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7592794b-83a6-4038-8f32-576b7f8ca303",
                                                "sense_id": "ca04ff37-2cae-3020-93fe-11b2d3666afa",
                                                "text": "Only an opaque and weak orthography-to-phonology analogy rule can be found with the phono-semantic compound type of characters (i.e., the xingshēng zi), which covers 80% of modern daily-use characters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74d9a85e-94ed-40bb-bee9-d317c16f31cc",
                                                "sense_id": "ca04ff37-2cae-3020-93fe-11b2d3666afa",
                                                "text": "'Jeon' is a phono-semantic compound which is formed from two elements of different words in two parts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "243d2cb1-7ca6-4aeb-b170-313d52da2d44",
                                                "sense_id": "ca04ff37-2cae-3020-93fe-11b2d3666afa",
                                                "text": "The Chinese character 城 is a phono-semantic compound of the \"place\" or \"earth\" radical 土 and 成, whose Old Chinese pronunciation has been reconstructed as *deŋ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3a16299-2657-4167-a49d-1a8b62274699",
                                                "sense_id": "ca04ff37-2cae-3020-93fe-11b2d3666afa",
                                                "text": "Phono-semantic compound characters, or the combination of elements that provide meaning and sound: the rebus 干 (gan) provides the phonetic basis for combinations with determinative characters such as 木 (mu, tree),日 (ri, sun), and 月 (rou, meat), to create the characters ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
